<title>THAILAND: Foreign brokers allowed three Thai partners - SET.</title>
<headline>Foreign brokers allowed three Thai partners - SET.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Thailand (SET) said on Tuesday it had approved a proposal to allow foreign brokers in Thailand to increase the number of local broking or sub-broking partners to three from two.</p>
<p>&quot;This is the first stage. In the near future we may liberalise his,&quot; said Sopawadee Lertmasnaschai, who heads the SET's examinations department.</p>
<p>&quot;The limit was set at two companies, now we have opened it up to one more.&quot; She said the decision made was considered final since it did not need approval from higher authorities.</p>
</text>
